  "revisions": {
    "2026-10-09": "Investor return timeline, monthly payment download, and investor one-sheet refreshed; master documents retained.",
    "2026-10-11": "Reconciled 687 cost rows and a 72-month stress forecast; audited authenticated Higgsfield usage and revised 102-minute media generation allowances; refreshed all six PDFs and current source documents. Business plan is 53 pages including the complete 44-page historical reference; Bible is 43 pages including 35 historical pages; operations companion is 125 pages including 117 historical pages. Historical financial claims are superseded; current debt service fails modeled coverage. Corrected digital navigation and motion runtime errors.",
    "2026-10-11-loan-pricing": "Repriced the current $1.5M full-draw loan illustration to proposed 12% fixed annual interest; refreshed payment schedules, forecast, PDFs and source documents; added primary-source pricing rationale and 10%/12%/14% sensitivity. Historical 9% cases remain superseded. All four modeled scenarios still fail debt coverage.",
    "2026-10-11-staged-financing": "Replaced immediate full-draw financing with a proposed maximum $1.5M staged commitment at 12% fixed interest on drawn principal only. First draw TBD; 24-month draw and interest-only period, followed by 84 amortizing months, final maturity month 108 with no term reset. Updated the 108-month forecast, calculator, five PDFs and current documents. Only 05_Investor_One_Sheet.pdf remains as the public one-sheet; obsolete one-sheets and 72-month schedules removed from active publication. Full-draw math is hypothetical, all four scenarios fail coverage, and cost records remain unchanged.",
    "2026-10-11-digital-reading-room": "Added an inline reading room for nine current documents and a searchable explorer for all 687 cost rows, 49 source records, original calculations, twelve-month expense allocations and all four 108-month cash scenarios. Linked the presentation, business plan, financial update and current one-sheet to the digital views. Source prices, management allowances and unviable debt coverage remain explicitly distinguished."
  },
